    "result_text": "The full suite passes (BUILD SUCCESS). Done.\n\n## Summary\n\nThe registration-date business-day rule now skips public holidays as well as weekends. I made a single, contained change to `BusinessDay.java` \u2014 the one place all three call sites already funnel through \u2014 so no other files were touched:\n\n- Added a private `HOLIDAYS` set with the five fixed dates (2026-01-01, 2026-01-26, 2026-04-25, 2026-12-25, 2026-12-28).\n- Extracted a tiny `isBusinessDay` predicate (weekday **and** not a holiday).\n- Simplified `rollForward` into a loop that advances one day until it lands on a business day \u2014 which naturally handles a holiday adjacent to a weekend rolling forward correctly.\n\n**Structural-impact notes:** only one file changed. Behaviour lives in a small new predicate rather than being piled into the existing method, and `rollForward` itself stays low-complexity (a single loop). `BusinessDay`'s surrounding class complexity (`WMC_other`) remains minimal, so the edit cost stays small.\n\nTests are green (`BUILD SUCCESS`), including the `holiday-business-day` acceptance test.",
